* staging is unnecessary complication of the version control system
* git
	* UI design is bad
	* main concepts to understand
		* DAG of nodes
		* nodes can be viewed as commits or changesets or snapshots
		* branches are [represented by] just pointers to nodes
		* "HEAD" is a pointer to a node or to a branch
			* when it points not to a branch then it is said to be "detached"
		* good video introduction about the basics
			* LearnThatStack: Git Will Finally Make Sense After This
				\ links-to external https://youtu.be/Ala6PHlYjmw?si=-hlAmC3f2Vzv5SQw
	* commands
		\ links-to internal qvfpcfhsrrkpbktn
	* how to
		* edit a deep changeset
			* 'git rebase -i'
			* 'git reset HEAD~'
				* do not omit "~" from the end of "HEAD"
		* deleting history
			* to save storage cost for github hosting a website
			* this algorithm deletes all the history
				* take the storage of the history away from git
					* mv .git .git-backup
				* create the repository like it would not exist before
					* git init
				* get back the configuration of the repository
					* cp .git-backup/config .git/config
				* create a first commit in the new history
					* git add --all git commit -m "1"
				* push this whole renewal of the history to the server
					* git push -u --force origin master
				* delete folder .git-backup
			* to delete only part of the history is also possible
				\ links-to external https://stackoverflow.com/questions/41953300/how-to-delete-the-old-git-history
	* folder layout
		* "working tree" - where the versioned data is
			* configure in git config file under section "core" as 'worktree = ...'
		* "git directory" - were the git data is
			* it is normally the ".git" folder but when not then a ".git" file takes its place, in which configure as "gitdir: ..."
		* other sources
			* Ooker on Stackoverflow
				\ links-to external https://stackoverflow.com/a/72586248
